    "quantifiers": "Universal E/S/V/kappa/measurable eta,y; source allpositive eta. One actual measurable p:S→E before all s, stationarity for all s and unique stationary z at each s. Every dependent rho/r/Z/q/f uses SAME p after fiberwise equality. No hidden reference point, eta cap, conditional selector certificate, or posterior-family Markov conclusion.",
    "assumptions": "Typing classes; source C2 and kappa>=1/normalized kappa^-1 I<=HessV<=I; eta positivity. Measurable eta/y and arbitrary S are disclosed authored representation extension (Unit recovers fixed source). No public probability/partition/moment/coherence/law/domain/LSI/canonical-Fisher/desired-bound certificate premise.",
    "conclusion": "Actual r_s probability and AC wrt gamma; canonical ENNReal klDiv(r_s,gamma)≠top; true gradientrho_s L2(r_s); finite KL.toReal<=1/2 integral norm gradientrho_s² under same r_s. This is sufficient KL/Fisher ingredient of printed FIRST4.6, not W2/T2 itself.",
    "scopes": "Authored integration node from actual32 domains, actual33 canonical entropy and actual42 sufficient noncompact C2 functionLSI. Source has no printed standalone named KL-half-Fisher theorem. No fullW12, smooth canonicalRN relativeFisher identity, Gaussian T2/W2/FIRST4.6, bias/fullLemma/main/cost/Markov posterior-family/composition/PURIFIED claim.",
    "constant_dependencies": "stdGaussian variance1; functionLSI2 times actual square-root gradient energy1/4 gives1/2. q mass exactly1 cancels masslogmass. No dimension factor, positivity of mass/finite canonicalKL internally produced, all eta>0 and rank0 retained; numericalprox eta<=1/(2beta) is separate excluded cost contract."
